{"title":"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems\">2002 AMC 12B #1</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems\">2002 AMC 10B #3</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic_mean\" title=\"Arithmetic mean\">arithmetic mean</a> of the nine numbers in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/4736e4db53709b4a7dbc1d0d126f067d1e361b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{9, 99, 999, 9999, \\ldots, 999999999\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"254\" height=\"18\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, all of whose digits are distinct. The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> doesn't contain the digit\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/6257fe2a6d8a14165596d045ec870d6fc8249ad5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 2 \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 4 \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 6 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"342\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We wish to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19b205da2e1ef6b4265bfdc2a4857699b97d0be9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9+99+\\cdots +999999999}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"199\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/c/e5cfc55ba78a57f94db7447526227b01954adedc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9(1+11+111+\\cdots +111111111)}{9}=123456789$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"378\" height=\"38\" />. This doesn't have the digit 0, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec361c7e9aeb3c86487803857531536c3380334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the final number is guaranteed to have the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f1eab6a674efc2895a271c337e80a77811ebcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 3, 5, 7, 9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> and that each of these digits can be paired with an even number adding up to 9. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec361c7e9aeb3c86487803857531536c3380334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"29\" /> can be taken out, with the other digits fulfilling divisibility by 9.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The arithmetic mean is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/0/0206cac7bcd0681097fc16845cda8d690a65c50e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(10^1-1)+(10^2-1)+\\ldots+(10^9-1)}{9}=\\frac{1111111101}{9}=123456789$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"532\" height=\"41\" />. So select <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec57a6373350472bd9be0c231923ceb315ae968.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"24\" />.\n~hastapasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Gn28B8I5eTg\">https://youtu.be/Gn28B8I5eTg</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/w0Q7LG7jdg8\">https://youtu.be/w0Q7LG7jdg8</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</s